<header class="masthead">
  <p class="wordmark" aria-label="Punk"><b>P</b><b>U</b><b>N</b><b>K</b></p>
  <h1><a href="{% url.home %}">{% app %}</a></h1>
  <p class="sticker">no entry</p>
</header>

<section>
  <h2>Sign-in failed</h2>
  <p><a href="{% url.home %}">Try again</a></p>
  <p class="note">
    No reason is shown here, and that is deliberate: a verifier that
    tells the far side which check it failed is telling an attacker which
    one to work on next. The code is in the application log, and
    <code>punk saml verify</code> will say the same thing about a saved
    response.
  </p>
</section>
